  "worked_solution": "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the divergence of $F$ is the scalar field given by\n\n$$\n\\text{div}\\,F=\u2207\\cdot F=\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}+\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2207\\cdot F & =\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}+\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y} \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(xy))+\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(xy) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}+x \\\\  & =\\frac{1+{x}^{2}}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
